    "contenu": "\n      <p>The madeleine is a star again. Long confined to childhood afternoon snacks, it now gets the full attention of the great Parisian pastry chefs: domed shell, generous hump, soft centre, sometimes a glaze or a molten heart. Here is our ranking of the <strong>best madeleines in Paris</strong>, with an openly stated note of transparency about our number one.</p>\n\n      <h2>1. Mado Paris, our partner, our best-seller</h2>\n      <p><strong>In the interest of transparency: Mado is our partner, so our opinion is not neutral.</strong> But if we chose it <strong>from our very beginnings</strong>, and exclusively, it is precisely because its madeleine convinced us before anyone else: a clear hump, a light, buttery crumb, and flawless consistency from one batch to the next. Since our beginnings it has been <strong>L'Écrin's best-seller</strong>: it is the product our clients talk about the day after a breakfast. Plain, lemon, pistachio-raspberry, chocolate… the Mado range lives up to all its promises, and it is the one we serve in our boxes and our office breakfasts.</p>\n\n      <h2>2. Gilles Marchal, in Montmartre</h2>\n      <p>In his shop on rue Ravignan, in Montmartre, Gilles Marchal offers madeleines made and baked on site several times a day, like the rest of his pastries.</p>\n\n      <h2>3. Blé Sucré, the cult glazed madeleine</h2>\n      <p>In the 12th arrondissement, Fabrice Le Bourdat popularised a madeleine with a thin lemon glaze that became a cult item. Crisp outside, melting inside: a Parisian classic. The shop is now run by Anne-Sophie Gesqua, who has taken over its classics, madeleines included.</p>\n\n      <h2>4. The Ritz, François Perret's haute couture version</h2>\n      <p>The Ritz's head pastry chef raised the madeleine to the rank of a palace dessert, with molten-centre versions served at the Comptoir du Ritz. An exceptional madeleine, worthy of the address.</p>\n\n      <h2>Why the madeleine is so popular in companies</h2>\n      <p>Individual format, no cutlery, instant generosity: the madeleine is the ideal sweet item for a breakfast or a team break. It is shared without any logistics and appeals to everyone. That is why it holds a central place in what we offer.</p>\n\n      <h2>Ordering Mado madeleines in Paris</h2>\n      <p>Our boxes of Mado madeleines (10, 20 or 50 pieces) and our office breakfasts are delivered from <strong>6:30 am</strong> in Paris and Île-de-France. <a href=\"/devis\">Request your quote</a> and serve your teams one of the best madeleines in the capital.</p>\n\n      <h2>Sources</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li>Gilles Marchal: <a href=\"https://www.gillesmarchal.com/\">official website</a>, accessed 15 October 2026.</li>\n        <li>Blé Sucré: <a href=\"https://www.gillespudlowski.com/?p=417834\">article by Gilles Pudlowski</a>, 8 February 2026.</li>\n        <li>The Ritz: <a href=\"https://bonjourparis.com/food-and-drink/francois-perret-the-madeleine-maestro-at-the-ritz-paris\">Bonjour Paris, profile of François Perret</a>.</li>\n        <li>Mado Paris: partner of L'Écrin Traiteur since our beginnings.</li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <h2>Frequently asked questions: madeleines in Paris</h2>\n      <div class=\"faq-block\">\n        <details>\n          <summary><strong>What are the best madeleines in Paris?</strong></summary>\n          <p>Among the references: Mado Paris, Gilles Marchal, Blé Sucré and the Ritz (François Perret). At L'Écrin, we serve Mado madeleines, our partner since our beginnings.</p>\n        </details>\n        <details>\n          <summary><strong>Can you have madeleines delivered to an office in Paris?</strong></summary>\n          <p>Yes. Our boxes of Mado madeleines (10, 20 or 50 pieces) and our breakfasts are delivered from 6:30 am in Paris and Île-de-France, on a simple quote.</p>\n        </details>\n        <details>\n          <summary><strong>Why is Mado your reference madeleine?</strong></summary>\n          <p>For its consistency, its generous hump and its buttery crumb. Chosen as our partner from our very beginnings, it has become L'Écrin's best-seller, praised by our clients.</p>\n        </details>\n      </div>\n    ",
